ch simulation, of course). This should provide\nL465@P2: accuracies of simulated FAPs about 1% for FAP = 0.1 and\nL466@P2: about 10% for FAP = 10−3. The simulated tale of FAP <\nL467@P2: 10−3often showed unstable deviations comparable with the\nL468@P2-3: false alarm probability.4 R.V. Baluev\nL469@P3:  1e-04\nL470@P3:  0.001\nL471@P3:  0.01\nL472@P3:  0.1\nL473@P3:  1\nL474@P3:  0 5 10 15 20\nL475@P3: max z(f)\nL476@P3: false alarm probability\nL477@P3: Simulated: N=1000, even\nL478@P3: Simulated: N=100, random\nL479@P3: Simulated: N=30, random\nL480@P3: Analytic: alias-free\nL481@P3: Analytic: Davies bound\n"
